{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars","id":759509,"title":"One Punch Man - the Dawn'est of Dawn Caste Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-06T17:00:07-08:00","id":759509,"title":"One Punch Man - the Dawn'est of Dawn Caste Solars","content":"Ok, first off: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GEKOaqF7C4w\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GEKOaqF7C4w</a><br /> <br /> Basically, tryhard alchy VS no-effort Solar with midling appearance<br /> <br /> <br /> Can we agree that One Punch Man is basically the Dawnest of Dawn Castes? And the cheesiest.<br /> <br /> I mean, super amazing powers, completely fearless (integrity charms are fun), and basically invulnerable - though I guess the main thing against it all is his apparent lack of heroic motivation.<br /> <br /> He is, after all, just a guy who plays hero for fun according to the show","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:14:51-08:00","id":759550,"title":"","content":"Saitama is a very Solar-y character, yeah<br /> <br /> And a good example of how Brawl doesn't mean just &quot;brutal thug&quot; but can mean &quot;transcendentally good fighter&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:26:22-08:00","id":759565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759550#post759550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saitama is a very Solar-y character, yeah<br /> <br /> And a good example of how Brawl doesn't mean just &quot;brutal thug&quot; but can mean &quot;transcendentally good fighter&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my players has a Twilight who uses Brawl. Not because she's a thug or because she habitually beats up people. She was raised as a monk, but the fighting style there wasn't &quot;Emulate the predatory spirit of the Tiger&quot; or &quot;Focus on the Single Perfect Strike&quot;. It was &quot;This is how you make a fist. Now, punch that log until your hands have been turned into weapons.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a LOT of room for types of Brawl, in my opinion. There's room for the guy who says &quot;Martial Arts? Man, fuck that noise. I learned to fight by <i>fighting</i>. Each scar and bruise on my body is a lesson learned while walking through the streets of my home.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's room for the monk who, rather than focus on the ideals of Snake Style, simply practiced one punch ten thousand times until they had perfected it... And moved on to other simple techniques. Their Brawl isn't the rough style of the streets, it's a very precise method derived from honing themselves.<br /> <br /> There's also room for the brawler who just improvises, and is good at clubbing people with buckets, stools, and other people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:53:48-08:00","id":759579,"title":"","content":"Saitama is also a good expression of the new non-stabby/War Dawn Caste Abilities I feel. He does a lot which feels like good expressions of Awareness, Dodge and Resistance, which shows how those Abilities together lead to interesting aesthetic results if that's your bag.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:00:05-08:00","id":759586,"title":"","content":"A dawn caste solar is not adequate to convey how badly Saitama breaks the power scales in his own universe. Maybe if you fused all the dawn caste exaltations into a single super exaltation it would be adequate to convey his hax. <i>Maybe</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:45:35-08:00","id":759623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759586#post759586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dawn caste solar is not adequate to convey how badly Saitama breaks the power scales in his own universe. Maybe if you fused all the dawn caste exaltations into a single super exaltation it would be adequate to convey his hax. <i>Maybe</i></div> </div> </div> </div>So... a second edition Solar with Essence 10?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T18:47:22-08:00","id":759624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759623#post759623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... a second edition Solar with Essence 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>With those Jon Cheung rewrites to Solar Hero Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:05:42-08:00","id":759634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759623#post759623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... a second edition Solar with Essence 10?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? That still would not be sufficient. We don't even know exactly how overpowered Saitama is yet because literally nothing has ever pushed him to his limit. The absolute most anyone has ever gotten out of him is 'not actively holding back but not really trying either'. At least an E10 2nd edition solar had other solars around to potentially match them and had beings like the Primordials who were (nominally) on the same level of power as them. Saitama would be a guy who came in and somehow smacked a primordial around without even spending any motes<br /> <br /> Edit: And for the record, the guy who got him to that level of effort was an alien warlord scouring the galaxy for someone that could give him a challenge because he himself was so insanely overpowered nobody could touch him. He could destroy a planet and at one point hit someone hard enough to send them flying all the way to the moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 11-06-2015, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:13:26-08:00","id":759638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759634#post759634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? That still would not be sufficient. We don't even know exactly how overpowered Saitama is yet because literally nothing has ever pushed him to his limit. The absolute most anyone has ever gotten out of him is 'not actively holding back but not really trying either'. At least an E10 2nd edition solar had other solars around to potentially match them and had beings like the Primordials who were (nominally) on the same level of power as them. Saitama would be a guy who came in and somehow smacked a primordial around without even spending any motes<br /> <br /> Edit: And for the record, the guy who got him to that level of effort was an alien warlord scouring the galaxy for someone that could give him a challenge because he himself was so insanely overpowered nobody could touch him. He could destroy a planet and at one point hit someone hard enough to send them flying all the way to the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>And your way of putting it can really drive home that people saying &quot;There's no way to make Superman interesting&quot; are full of crap. Yes, yes there are. You have to explore Superman's mindset, you have to really try, but you CAN make Superman stories very interesting and compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T19:19:47-08:00","id":759642,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was pretty skeptical when someone recommended it to me and told me the premise but I love it. I'm glad the people doing the anime are handling it so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:09:46-08:00","id":759661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759634#post759634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? That still would not be sufficient. We don't even know exactly how overpowered Saitama is yet because literally nothing has ever pushed him to his limit. The absolute most anyone has ever gotten out of him is 'not actively holding back but not really trying either'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we want to go for comparisons here. E.g. &quot;2E Essence 10 Solar in a World of Darkness game&quot; level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:43:28-08:00","id":759676,"title":"","content":"If Saitama was an Exalted character, he'd be a mortal. And he'd one-shot Solar player characters with transperfect punches, so that the storyteller could laugh at them.<br /> <br /> His power source is humour + author fiat. That's why he can splatter monsters, yet fail to swat a mosquito.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:50:06-08:00","id":759677,"title":"","content":"If you want to use World of Darkness then he would be the guy who walked up to Cain and his 'you lose' stat sheet and kicked his ass so hard the thinnest blooded of the kindred would feel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","user":"Mizu","date":". 11-07-2015, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T20:54:45-08:00","id":759685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759634#post759634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? That still would not be sufficient. We don't even know exactly how overpowered Saitama is yet because literally nothing has ever pushed him to his limit. The absolute most anyone has ever gotten out of him is 'not actively holding back but not really trying either'. At least an E10 2nd edition solar had other solars around to potentially match them and had beings like the Primordials who were (nominally) on the same level of power as them. Saitama would be a guy who came in and somehow smacked a primordial around without even spending any motes<br /> <br /> Edit: And for the record, the guy who got him to that level of effort was an alien warlord scouring the galaxy for someone that could give him a challenge because he himself was so insanely overpowered nobody could touch him. He could destroy a planet and at one point hit someone hard enough to send them flying all the way to the moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Sounds like cheap 2e perfects to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:33:17-08:00","id":759842,"title":"","content":"Yes, One Punch Man is indeed a strong demonstration of how terribly dull it is to be able to defeat everything with virtually no risk or effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T02:48:12-08:00","id":759846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759842#post759842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, One Punch Man is indeed a strong demonstration of how terribly dull it is to be able to defeat everything with virtually no risk or effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the problem with text and a lack of reference.<br /> <br /> In a straight-forward reading, Isator is criticizing the cartoon. He finds it dull because it lacks the drama of overcoming obstacles. At the same time, Isator does sometimes use dry, ironic humor. It's possible that he finds the cartoon very good, and is making a facetious comment.<br /> <br /> If I knew the show, I could judge for myself, but I've never seen it.<br /> <br /> It's Schrodinger's sarcasm. Where you've been on the internet so long, your brain can no longer reconcile while a statement is sincere or not. Rather, all statements exist in within the possibility of whether they mean what they say or mean the very opposite of what they say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:14:13-08:00","id":759851,"title":"","content":"If that's a Solar vs Alchemical....?<br /> <br /> Road Runner vs Wile E Coyote = Solar Beastman with Dodge vs Lunar? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:16:03-08:00","id":759853,"title":"","content":"Having read OPM it's probably a serious statement - Saitama is bored out of his skull because nothing challenges him, being overpowered as all get-out. The comic is in large part an exploration of that concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/855-magistrate","name":"Magistrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T03:42:56-08:00","id":759868,"title":"","content":"I was actually mostly using it as a reference to make a jab at Second Edition combat. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I wouldn't say the show itself is dull so much as it's about somebody's experience of a dull thing, which isn't bad (although I find the continuous bait-and-switch of setting up what looks like a thrilling action sequence with an abrupt ending to be a bit of a misfire), but doesn't do much for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T04:08:18-08:00","id":759882,"title":"","content":"Man, I was going to make the exact same thread.<br /> <br /> Saitama is an elder-essence Solar, so OP that no one can face him, so bored out of his skull that Creation oughta be afraid of what he'll do to entertain himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T13:52:49-08:00","id":760190,"title":"","content":"Can I just give a shout out to how the dream sequence fight in the first episode is everything I could want from exalted level combat? Definitely want to use those subterranean people and their king for demon visuals now....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8807-galatine","name":"Galatine","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T23:20:53-08:00","id":760526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>God_of_Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=759882#post759882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I was going to make the exact same thread.<br /> <br /> Saitama is an elder-essence Solar, so OP that no one can face him, so bored out of his skull that Creation oughta be afraid of what he'll do to entertain himself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how Dreams of the First Age was setting up scene-long perfects with elder essence, it's totally this. The guy sounds like he has perfect attacks, defenses, and damage effects coming out of his ears, to the point where his fights are &quot;Do you have keyword X? If not, then lose spectacularly.&quot; I'm amused by how it almost perfectly embodied what was wrong with 2e keywords and perfects.<br /> <br /> E10 Solar hanging out with regular Dragon-Blooded would end that way. &quot;Sure you're heroes. Yay for you. I can literally beat you in my sleep. No really, I took a Charm to fight in my sleep so I didn't have to pay attention to beating you. I am. So. BORED.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:23:00-08:00","id":760563,"title":"","content":"Nah. Saitama is not only far too powerful for the rpg scale to quantify (which is part of the joke), but he has very little of the Solar thing except for being really powerful. Solars are these god-kings larger than life that return and everyone needs to acknowledge and all that crap. Saitama is a caped baldy nobody except Genos respects, who is a hero as a hobby, and lives in a tiny run-down apartment while reading manga and worrying about bake sales. I've been mightily yelled at in this very forum for suggesting characters far less &quot;mundane&quot; than Saitama as Exalted.<br /> <br /> Saitama is the most normal dude in a world full of Exalted characters, who has power beyond any of all the larger than life mega-heroes that would normally be protagonists and such simply because it's funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T01:39:44-08:00","id":760572,"title":"","content":"There are a couple people besides Genos that respect Saitama like he deserves. Still few enough that they can be counted on one hand, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T02:07:20-08:00","id":760574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760572#post760572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple people besides Genos that respect Saitama like he deserves. Still few enough that they can be counted on one hand, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bang, and who else? I mean, King likes Saitama and enjoys his company, but what they have isn't exactly the kind of respect Genos and Bang have for Saitama. It's more two total nerds being friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T03:22:26-08:00","id":760586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760574#post760574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bang, and who else? I mean, King likes Saitama and enjoys his company, but what they have isn't exactly the kind of respect Genos and Bang have for Saitama. It's more two total nerds being friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bang, Sonic, King (he knows Saitama is the guy who actually did the stuff people attributed to him), licenseless Rider, and Fubuki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T03:38:19-08:00","id":760591,"title":"","content":"Watched the 5 episodes whcih are subbed, yesterday (and props to this thread for that). Pretty cool. Really creative animation and vibrant designs, comedy gore, it really will parody anything, and it zips along at a fair old pace with absolutely no filler at all.<br /> <br /> About his Solarness, Saitama seems a hero who just trained and trained and unlocked his potential himself and is *just* a human (&quot;Humans don't fly&quot; when asked why he doesn't fly!). So that's like Solars... At the same time, he kind of seems to playfully parody with skepticism the idea of people just unlocking their potential by effort (100 push ups, 100 sit ups, 100 squats, 10 km run!) in a way that Solars just play with more unironic sincerity. And he's so socially apathetic, not a character whose fits burn with rage for social justice! But then yeah, it is seem like, partly, a parody of shounen. Different genres do not translate 100% (or even 50%, 20%...)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T04:19:58-08:00","id":760603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760586#post760586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bang, Sonic, King (he knows Saitama is the guy who actually did the stuff people attributed to him), licenseless Rider, and Fubuki.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about Licenseless Rider. But unless more has happened in the ONE webcomic (I follow the Murata redraw), saying that Fubuki &quot;respects&quot; Saitama strikes me as rather an exaggeration :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T06:53:14-08:00","id":760642,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, Licenceless Rider, who's power is to carry the pair of tiny neutron stars he calls his balls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T07:39:28-08:00","id":760660,"title":"","content":"Folks I think are getting a bit tied-up into an idea that &quot;Good inspiration&quot; means &quot;I could import it without any changes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Saitama doesn't fit Exalted as he is in the show in regards to his power level. He is still a good inspiration though in I think a lot of the aesthetic to how he is as as an athlete and dude who can fight and how those manifest in how he fights. So in that regard he's a rather comedic (and extreme) demonstration of a lot of the Dawn Caste Abilities I think, namely Awareenss, Brawl, Dodge and Resistance, plus some Athletics and Integrity tossed in, I think.<br /> <br /> He isn't really usable as he is presented in his universe, but he is fairly cool inpsiration for what to think on with making Solars in Creation.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T08:09:45-08:00","id":760669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760660#post760660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Folks I think are getting a bit tied-up into an idea that &quot;Good inspiration&quot; means &quot;I could import it without any changes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Saitama doesn't fit Exalted as he is in the show in regards to his power level. He is still a good inspiration though in I think a lot of the aesthetic to how he is as as an athlete and dude who can fight and how those manifest in how he fights. So in that regard he's a rather comedic (and extreme) demonstration of a lot of the Dawn Caste Abilities I think, namely Awareenss, Brawl, Dodge and Resistance, plus some Athletics and Integrity tossed in, I think.<br /> <br /> He isn't really usable as he is presented in his universe, but he is fairly cool inpsiration for what to think on with making Solars in Creation.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, what I'm saying, at least, is that Saitama is extremely at odds from a thematic level with Exalted. Exalted is not about how people earn power, but about people who want to apply it and shake the world to its foundations and so on.<br /> <br /> Saitama worked his ass raw to get power... and has no idea what to do with it. He never did. He has no ambition, and no overriding drive - he could do anything he wanted with all the power he has, but it would never pass his mind for an instant, and even if you suggested it to him, he'd blow it off as &quot;a hassle&quot;. He'd rather spend his time playing Idolmaster in his PSP than performing heroics, and his worries are for groceries and rent money. He is, in fact, the exact <i>opposite </i>of everything the devs tell us an Exalt should be, except for being strong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","user":"Drascin","date":". 11-08-2015, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T08:44:09-08:00","id":760684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760669#post760669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, what I'm saying, at least, is that Saitama is extremely at odds from a thematic level with Exalted. Exalted is not about how people earn power, but about people who want to apply it and shake the world to its foundations and so on.<br /> <br /> Saitama worked his ass raw to get power... and has no idea what to do with it. He never did. He has no ambition, and no overriding drive - he could do anything he wanted with all the power he has, but it would never pass his mind for an instant, and even if you suggested it to him, he'd blow it off as &quot;a hassle&quot;. He'd rather spend his time playing Idolmaster in his PSP than performing heroics, and his worries are for groceries and rent money. He is, in fact, the exact <i>opposite </i>of everything the devs tell us an Exalt should be, except for being strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that's why I consdier him more an aesthetic than an actual cahracter inspiration. He's good to draw on for when fights go extreme and such I feel. At least until he unceremoniously ends them, mind. But I like his dodging and taking things to the face at least<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:41:50-08:00","id":760901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760669#post760669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, what I'm saying, at least, is that Saitama is extremely at odds from a thematic level with Exalted. Exalted is not about how people earn power, but about people who want to apply it and shake the world to its foundations and so on.<br /> <br /> Saitama worked his ass raw to get power... and has no idea what to do with it. He never did. He has no ambition, and no overriding drive - he could do anything he wanted with all the power he has, but it would never pass his mind for an instant, and even if you suggested it to him, he'd blow it off as &quot;a hassle&quot;. He'd rather spend his time playing Idolmaster in his PSP than performing heroics, and his worries are for groceries and rent money. He is, in fact, the exact <i>opposite </i>of everything the devs tell us an Exalt should be, except for being strong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. Exalted doesn't require that Solars have a constant unrelenting drive; it's something that frequently characterizes them, yes, but they can also be Achilles in his tent.<br /> <br /> And Saitama isn't meant to be one of those starting Solars; he's an E5 Solar who has climbed the peak of the world and now has no idea what to do with himself. He was incredibly driven earlier in his life, but now he's achieved all his goals and found them empty. If that's not a valid concept for an older Solar, then something is wrong with the game.<br /> <br /> (Keep in mind that Saitama's ennui is because the world has ceased to challenge him. If he found a worthy opponent, he would become driven again.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 11-08-2015, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T14:56:09-08:00","id":760962,"title":"","content":"Invincible champion of war... regards anything other than playing games as a hassle and is irritated by guys turning and wanting to be his disciple.... Saitama is clearly the Unconquered Sun! (&quot;A guy who is the Supreme God of the World just for fun.&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T15:39:11-08:00","id":760986,"title":"","content":"Well, if nothing else Genos is a cool Alchemical. A bit too much straight up tech for my liking in Exalted, but Alchemicals have always had that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T16:51:59-08:00","id":761042,"title":"","content":"Translating characters to Exalted is tricky. Translating characters to something like Mutants and Masterminds is easier as it's basically an open system with a lot of room or players to design powers and such. Exalted has certain setting assumptions and divisions (like Castes) which can make translating characters tricky.<br /> <br /> Still, Saitama is basically an Essence 10, Second Edition Solar with maximum combat traits hanging out in the Classic World of Darkness - &quot;Oh, Antedeluvian?&quot; *Yawn* *Punch*. &quot;Oh, Wyrm Talon?&quot; *Yawn* *Punch*<br /> <br /> Genos is an Alchemical as mentioned earlier. Some of the other characters can be roughly translated. Tatsumaki as a Defiler who maxed out all of the Mind Hand Charms and has some Malfeas, &quot;I'm the best&quot; charms for Integrity and such. Garou could work as a Lunar, though that may depend on what direction the authors take Lunars in the new edition. Child Emperor is a low Essence Twilight with Supernal Craft. Zombieman is a Liminal.<br /> <br /> And then there are some that are in odd places like Pig God, or whom I can only peg as an Exigent, or characters like Speed of Sound Sonic who could be a Solar, abyssal, or possibly even a high Essence Air Aspect.<br /> <br /> Regardless of actually translating characters, I imagine Onepunch Man will often show up in threads about material for Exalted inspirations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T16:06:06-08:00","id":763555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=760603#post760603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forgot about Licenseless Rider. But unless more has happened in the ONE webcomic (I follow the Murata redraw), saying that Fubuki &quot;respects&quot; Saitama strikes me as rather an exaggeration :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, maybe respect is a bit too strong. But she acknowledges he is a super powerful freak of nature as opposed to thinking he is some sort of fraud or joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T20:47:22-08:00","id":763721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/759509-one-punch-man-the-dawn-est-of-dawn-caste-solars?p=763555#post763555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, maybe respect is a bit too strong. But she acknowledges he is a super powerful freak of nature as opposed to thinking he is some sort of fraud or joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tatsumaki, going by her dialogue at the end of her and Saitama's fight in the ONE manga seems to also respect him.<br /> <br /> In her own way, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}